{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"35":{"eng-name":"Combing the Hair (Kitab Al-Tarajjul)","ara-name":"كتاب الترجل"}},"section_detail":{"35":{"hadithnumber_first":4159,"hadithnumber_last":4213,"arabicnumber_first":4159,"arabicnumber_last":4213}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":4204,"arabicnumber":4204,"text":"Rapporté par Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah رضي الله عنه : Le jour de la conquête de La Mecque, on amena Abu Quhafah dont la tête et la barbe étaient blanches comme l’hysope. Le Messager d’Allah ﷺ a dit : « Changez cela, mais évitez le noir. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim (2102)"}],"reference":{"book":35,"hadith":46},"chapter":{"id":18,"ara-name":"باب فِي الْخِضَابِ","eng-name":"Dyeing Hair","isFirstHadith":false}}]}